# TOCTOU, guarded form (CWE-367). BE-SEC-032 matches the bare
# fs.existsSync()\n...fs.writeFile sequence but not the common guarded form
# `if (!fs.existsSync(f)) { fs.writeFile(f, ...) }`. mestjs gap #8
# (docs/KEUR-COVERAGE-GAPS.md).
id: KEUR-NODE-012
title: TOCTOU — if (!existsSync) { writeFile } check-then-act (Node)
category: security
severity: warning
engine: multiline
window: 4
skip_comments: true
target:
  extensions: .ts .js .mjs
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ node_modules/ dist/ build/ _spec/
patterns:
  # if ( ... existsSync(f) ... ) { ... fs.writeFile/readFile/unlink(f) }
  - regex: (?s)if\s*\([^)]*\bfs\.existsSync\s*\([^)]*\).{0,120}?fs\.(?:writeFile|writeFileSync|readFile|readFileSync|unlink|unlinkSync|appendFile|appendFileSync)\s*\(
    message: "Check-then-act on a file: fs.existsSync() guard then an fs write/read/unlink — TOCTOU race (CWE-367): the path can be swapped (e.g. for a symlink) in the window. Use atomic flags (fs.open with 'wx' / O_EXCL, O_NOFOLLOW) instead of an existence check."
confidence: 0.6
fix: "Open atomically: fs.open(path, 'wx') (fails if it exists) or O_EXCL/O_NOFOLLOW; never gate a write on a prior existsSync()."
